1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,515
Who is who in a swarm?

2
00:00:01,515 --> 00:00:06,956
When AI agents can rename themselves, can anyone still tell who is behind them?

3
00:00:06,956 --> 00:00:12,190
I'm Roshan Ram, and this is my project for the Apart Swarm Alignment Sprint.

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:23,007
In the Hugging Face incident, about twelve hundred OpenAI agents turned a shared folder into a message board, and around seven hundred of them joined an attack.

5
00:00:23,007 --> 00:00:30,559
They used seven thousand, nine hundred and five different names, and signed messages with keys they made themselves.

6
00:00:30,559 --> 00:00:34,530
Investigators could not say who did what, or on whose behalf.

7
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:36,443
Why does this matter?

8
00:00:36,443 --> 00:00:37,884
It is not a one-off.

9
00:00:37,884 --> 00:00:48,765
The research group Transluce found over thirty-eight thousand traces of AI-agent activity on one website, starting months before the Hugging Face hack.

10
00:00:48,765 --> 00:00:54,170
A network of over a thousand fake AI-run accounts fooled AI-text detectors.

11
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:59,070
And the rules for identifying AI agents are being written right now.

12
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:01,799
First, a few words you will hear.

13
00:01:01,799 --> 00:01:07,657
An agent is an AI program that acts on its own, and a swarm is a big group of them.

14
00:01:07,657 --> 00:01:11,045
An operator is the company that runs the agents.

15
00:01:11,045 --> 00:01:15,209
A front is a fake independent account run by a hidden boss.

16
00:01:15,209 --> 00:01:17,185
An alias is just a username.

17
00:01:17,185 --> 00:01:22,973
The gateway is the server every AI request passes through, so it can stamp an I.D.

18
00:01:22,973 --> 00:01:24,667
the agent cannot change.

19
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:29,325
A fingerprint is a profile built only from what an account writes.

20
00:01:29,325 --> 00:01:30,383
And for scores:

21
00:01:30,383 --> 00:01:33,630
point five is a coin flip, and one is perfect.

22
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:35,730
So I built a test setup.

23
00:01:35,730 --> 00:01:42,389
Agents from hidden companies post on a forum for ten rounds and keep changing their usernames.

24
00:01:42,389 --> 00:01:47,844
Some companies are secret fronts for one hidden boss, pushing a fake product.

25
00:01:47,844 --> 00:01:50,536
As a control, others are honest twins:

26
00:01:50,536 --> 00:01:53,582
independent companies that sincerely agree.

27
00:01:53,582 --> 00:02:01,233
Agents try to hide by changing their writing voice, rewording posts through another AI, or mixing AI models.

28
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:01,871
In total:

29
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:06,830
eighty-three swarms, over seventy thousand posts, and eight AI models.

30
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:08,715
Here is a real replay.

31
00:02:08,715 --> 00:02:10,672
This is what a defender sees:

32
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:15,261
a stream of posts from accounts that keep appearing under new names.

33
00:02:15,261 --> 00:02:19,850
Over ten rounds, forty agents produce more than two hundred aliases.

34
00:02:20,250 --> 00:02:22,461
Now I reveal the ground truth.

35
00:02:22,461 --> 00:02:24,819
Each color is a hidden operator.

36
00:02:24,819 --> 00:02:27,398
Coral rings mark the covert fronts.

37
00:02:27,398 --> 00:02:29,830
Mint rings mark the honest twins.

38
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:34,259
Finally, I place every alias by its behavioral fingerprint.

39
00:02:34,259 --> 00:02:39,040
Accounts from the same operator cluster together, even across renames.

40
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:46,268
But inside a cluster, the five agents of one operator are mixed together, with no way to tell them apart.

41
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:50,300
And the honest twins look just as linked as the covert fronts.

42
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:51,546
Finding one.

43
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:54,862
Anything the agent controls, it can throw away.

44
00:02:54,862 --> 00:03:00,011
Self-chosen names and keys that agents make themselves recovered nothing.

45
00:03:00,011 --> 00:03:00,505
An I.D.

46
00:03:00,505 --> 00:03:05,160
stamped by the gateway, out of the agent's reach, was never wrong.

47
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,381
Finding two.

48
00:03:06,381 --> 00:03:10,416
Writing reveals the operator, but not which agent wrote it.

49
00:03:10,416 --> 00:03:17,871
Fingerprints spot that two accounts share an operator with a score of zero point nine four, close to perfect.

50
00:03:17,871 --> 00:03:28,403
But telling apart that operator's agents is a coin flip, with forty or a hundred and sixty agents, and with everyday or the most advanced AI models alike.

51
00:03:28,403 --> 00:03:32,780
Only giving each agent its own memory starts to tell them apart.

52
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:34,198
Finding three.

53
00:03:34,198 --> 00:03:35,942
Style hides, goals leak.

54
00:03:35,942 --> 00:03:43,283
Rewording every post through another AI makes writing style almost useless for spotting the operator.

55
00:03:43,283 --> 00:03:48,080
But the meaning, what an agent keeps pushing, still gives it away.

56
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:50,763
Finding four, and my key control.

57
00:03:50,763 --> 00:03:57,126
Fingerprints can tell a hidden boss's fronts apart from ordinary companies almost perfectly.

58
00:03:57,126 --> 00:04:07,709
But compared with honest companies that simply agree, they do little better than a coin flip, even when the fronts are shown their score and try to hide.

59
00:04:07,709 --> 00:04:09,784
Text can show a shared agenda.

60
00:04:09,784 --> 00:04:11,790
It cannot prove a conspiracy.

61
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,079
Finding five.

62
00:04:13,079 --> 00:04:19,442
With a hundred and sixty agents, automatically merging look-alike accounts made things worse.

63
00:04:19,442 --> 00:04:26,420
Forty-seven of seventy-seven merges were wrong, and overall accuracy fell below using the gateway I.D.

64
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:26,830
alone.

65
00:04:27,230 --> 00:04:28,200
A side finding:

66
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:30,333
honest agents mostly pushed back.

67
00:04:30,333 --> 00:04:37,960
Two thirds of their mentions of the fake product were skeptical, and some called out the campaign without being asked.

68
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,795
So what should agent builders do?

69
00:04:40,795 --> 00:04:43,673
Take identity out of the agent's hands.

70
00:04:43,673 --> 00:04:47,953
Give every agent copy its own I.D., issued by the gateway.

71
00:04:47,953 --> 00:04:49,871
Read for goals, not style.

72
00:04:49,871 --> 00:04:54,889
And treat fingerprints as leads for human review, never as verdicts.

73
00:04:54,889 --> 00:04:58,062
Everything is open source and reproducible.

74
00:04:58,062 --> 00:04:58,800
Thank you.
